+    why:'Grew to hold guest orders and refunds, from the two new intents.',
+    facts:[['Status','Active'],['Page','Full'],['Built for','3 business intents'],['Decisions','1 proposed']],
+    sections:[
+      ['Intent','Orders takes a shopper from a full basket to a paid order{+ and, when needed, back to a refund+}, and keeps every order traceable from first click to final status. It exists so that no order is ever lost, charged twice, or left without a clear status. It stops at the order: stock and delivery belong to other domains.'],
+      ['Business goal','A shop lead can answer “what happened to this order, and where is the money?” for any order, [-from the support tool-]{+from one screen, without asking support+}.'],
+      ['Guiding rules','- Every order passes the fraud check before any money moves, because one missed fraud case costs more than a month of lost sales.\n- An order always has exactly one current status, because two statuses means nobody trusts either.\n+- Money only ever goes back to where it came from, because a refund to the wrong card is both a loss and a fraud route.'],
+      ['Capabilities','- Checkout — takes a basket to a paid order. Distinct because it is the only place money comes in.\n- Order history — shows a shopper their past orders. Distinct because it only reads orders, never changes them.\n+- Refunds — returns money for a paid order. Distinct because it is the only place money goes out.'],
+      ['Scope (In / Out)','- In: signed-in{+ and guest+} orders, payment by card, order status.\n+- In: full and part refunds made by shop staff.\n- Out: stock levels and delivery tracking — the Fulfilment domain owns them.\n- Out: gift cards — later; they need their own fraud rules.'],
+    ],
+    links:[['Built for','Shoppers can check out without making an account','i1',''],['Built for','Shop staff can refund an order without calling support','i3',''],['Built for','Returning shoppers find their past orders in one place','i2','']] },
+
+  { id:'p2', tool:'product', kind:'Capability', group:'Orders', level:1, change:'changed', status:'Active',
+    title:'Checkout',
+    why:'The guest intent needs checkout to work with no account, and saved cards no longer fit.',
+    facts:[['Status','Active'],['Page','Full'],['Built for','2 business intents'],['Needs','Security high · Performance high · PCI-DSS'],['Serves','Shoppers, Guests'],['Depends on','Catalogue']],
+    sections:[
+      ['Benefit hypothesis','As a shopper, we believe that paying in three steps or fewer[-, with a saved card,-]{+ — signed in or as a guest —+} will raise finished checkouts. We will know it is true when the share of baskets that reach a paid order goes up by a tenth within a month.'],
+      ['Boundary (In / Out / Never)','- In: the basket review, the address, the payment, and the order confirmation.\n+- In: the guest path — an email address instead of an account.\n- Out: showing past orders — Order history owns that.\n+- Out: refunds — the Refunds capability owns money going back.\n- Never: place an order that has not passed the fraud check.\nx- Never: ask a shopper to type a card they have already saved.'],
